  "summary": "I'm a soon-to-be alumni with extensive experience in software design and development. Programming is a love of mine: I enjoy building software to automate or simplify tasks. I've spent much of my college career working on lengthy projects for classes, my senior project, or independent development for my part time job as a grader. \n\nMany of the project I've worked on have been team project. In all of them, I've assumed the role of leader (or, for larger projects, \"prototype\" leader). This has given me experience in how to manage teams of developers, along with assessing tasks to be done and setting deadlines for work completion. \n\nBut I'm not just some programmer-for-hire-in-a-cubical. My goal is  to work in areas where I can develop software with a group of people. I want to be part of teams that build large products for large companies. Teams help foster innovation, and I like being part of that process with a group of colleagues I respect and enjoy working with.\n\nSpecialties: Software development; project management",
